        "original_id": "cc0854e4-31b0-5733-91a1-bd31b06400b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Norman L. Buckley, Peter Paige, Bradley Bredeweg, I. Marlene King, Tyler Blackburn\n- TV Series: The Fosters, The O.C., Chuck, Gossip Girl, Pretty Little Liars, Ravenswood\n- Episodes: Miss Me × 100\n- Networks: Freeform, ABC Family\n- Roles: television director, editor, showrunner\n\nFacts:\n- Norman L. Buckley was born on November 25, 1955, and he is an American television director and editor.\n- Norman L. Buckley is best known for his work on The O.C., Chuck, Gossip Girl, Pretty Little Liars, and The Fosters.\n- The Fosters was created by Peter Paige and Bradley Bredeweg.\n- The Fosters premiered in the United States on June 3, 2013, on the television network Freeform, which was previously named ABC Family.\n- The Pretty Little Liars episode Miss Me × 100 was directed by Norman Buckley and written by showrunner I. Marlene King.\n- Miss Me × 100 features the return of Tyler Blackburn as Caleb Rivers after his first episode absence since he left in the fourth season for the sister show Ravenswood.",
